From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OKO <oko@localhost>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] BLD: do not execute target numpy during cross build

Yocto already supplies numpy_inc_dir explicitly for class-target.

Do not invoke nativepython3 and attempt to import the target NumPy
package. Target extension modules are not build-host executables and
may fail or terminate with SIGILL.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [Yocto cross-build specific]
---
 pandas/meson.build | 29 ++++-------------------------
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 25 deletions(-)

diff --git a/pandas/meson.build b/pandas/meson.build
index 2c3423e..1234567 100644
--- a/pandas/meson.build
+++ b/pandas/meson.build
@@ -1,27 +1,6 @@
-incdir_numpy = run_command(
-    py,
-    [
-        '-c',
-        '''
-import os
-try:
-    import numpy as np
-    base_incdir = np.get_include()
-except Exception:
-    base_incdir = os.getenv('NUMPY_INC_DIR')
-
-try:
-    # Check if include directory is inside the pandas dir
-    # e.g. a venv created inside the pandas dir
-    # If so, convert it to a relative path
-    incdir = os.path.relpath(base_incdir)
-except Exception:
-    incdir = base_incdir
-print(incdir)
-     ''',
-    ],
-    env: {'NUMPY_INC_DIR': get_option('numpy_inc_dir')},
-    check: true,
-).stdout().strip()
+incdir_numpy = get_option('numpy_inc_dir')
+if incdir_numpy == ''
+    error('numpy_inc_dir must be specified when cross-compiling pandas')
+endif
 
 inc_np = include_directories(incdir_numpy)
 inc_pd = include_directories('_libs/include')
-- 
